const e='---\ntitle: "Minimal Checkout Bridge API"\ndescription: "Use the minimal theme as an external checkout bridge for creating orders, redirecting users to payment, and receiving paid callbacks."\n---\n\n# Minimal Checkout Bridge API\n\nThis document describes the external checkout bridge implemented under the `minimal` theme.\n\nIt is designed for this flow:\n\n1. Your external system creates a local APayShop order through an API call.\n2. APayShop returns a checkout URL.\n3. The user opens that URL and completes payment on the APayShop payment page.\n4. After payment succeeds, APayShop sends a server-to-server notification to your `notifyUrl`.\n5. The browser can also be redirected back to your `returnUrl` or `cancelUrl`.\n\n## Endpoints\n\n- `POST /api/minimal/checkout/create`\n- `GET /api/minimal/checkout/consume?token=...`\n- `GET /api/minimal/checkout/status`\n\n## Secret Configuration\n\nThe bridge uses a shared secret from one of the following sources:\n\n- setting key: `minimal_checkout_secret`\n- environment variable: `MINIMAL_CHECKOUT_SECRET`\n\nIf neither is configured, signed API requests will return `503`.\n\n## Signed Request Rules\n\nThe `create` and `status` endpoints require these request headers:\n\n```http\nX-APayShop-Timestamp: 1721712345678\nX-APayShop-Signature: <hex-hmac-sha256>\n```\n\nTimestamp must be within 5 minutes of the server time.\n\n### Signature Base For `create` And `status`\n\nThe signature is computed as:\n\n```text\nHMAC_SHA256(secret, timestamp + "\\n" + method + "\\n" + path_with_sorted_query + "\\n" + sha256(raw_body))\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- `method` is uppercased, for example `POST` or `GET`\n- `path_with_sorted_query` excludes any `signature` query parameter\n- query parameters must be sorted by key, then by value\n- `raw_body` is the exact raw request body string\n- for `GET /status`, use the SHA-256 of an empty string when there is no body\n\n## Create Checkout Order\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/minimal/checkout/create`\n\n### Request Body Example\n\n```json\n{\n  "externalOrderId": "EXT-20260723-0001",\n  "productId": 12,\n  "customerEmail": "buyer@example.com",\n  "notifyUrl": "https://merchant.example.com/api/payment/notify",\n  "returnUrl": "https://merchant.example.com/payment/success",\n  "cancelUrl": "https://merchant.example.com/payment/cancel",\n  "attach": {\n    "userId": "u_1024",\n    "channel": "mobile_h5"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `externalOrderId` | string | Yes | Merchant-side unique order number used for idempotency. |\n| `productId` | number | Yes | APayShop product ID. |\n| `customerEmail` | string | No | Buyer contact email. |\n| `notifyUrl` | string | No | Server-to-server callback URL after payment succeeds. |\n| `returnUrl` | string | No | Browser redirect target after successful payment. |\n| `cancelUrl` | string | No | Browser redirect target after cancellation or failed return. |\n| `attach` | object | No | Arbitrary passthrough data returned in `status` and `notifyUrl` payloads. |\n\n### Response Example\n\n```json\n{\n  "code": 0,\n  "message": "Checkout order created",\n  "data": {\n    "orderId": "ON20260723981234AB12CD34",\n    "externalOrderId": "EXT-20260723-0001",\n    "checkoutUrl": "https://yourdomain.com/api/minimal/checkout/consume?token=...",\n    "amount": 99,\n    "currency": "CNY",\n    "reused": false,\n    "clientIp": "203.0.113.10",\n    "expiresAt": "2026-07-23T13:05:00.000Z"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Idempotency\n\n`externalOrderId` is treated as the merchant-side idempotency key.\n\nIf the same `externalOrderId` is sent again:\n\n- the existing APayShop order is reused\n- a fresh `checkoutUrl` is returned\n- response field `data.reused` becomes `true`\n\nThe request will return `409` if the existing order conflicts with the new request, for example:\n\n- different `productId`\n- different `customerEmail`\n- different `notifyUrl`\n- different `returnUrl`\n- different `cancelUrl`\n\n## Consume Checkout URL\n\n**Endpoint:** `GET /api/minimal/checkout/consume?token=...`\n\nThis endpoint is intended for the browser only.\n\nIt validates the one-time checkout token, restores the correct `visitor_id` cookie, and redirects the browser to the built-in payment page:\n\n```text\n/payment/{orderId}\n```\n\nYou usually do not call this endpoint from your server. Open the returned `checkoutUrl` directly in the browser.\n\n## Query Payment Status\n\n**Endpoint:** `GET /api/minimal/checkout/status`\n\nSupports either:\n\n- `orderId`\n- `externalOrderId`\n\nAt least one of them is required.\n\n### Query Example\n\n```http\nGET /api/minimal/checkout/status?externalOrderId=EXT-20260723-0001\n```\n\n### Response Example\n\n```json\n{\n  "code": 0,\n  "data": {\n    "orderId": "ON20260723981234AB12CD34",\n    "externalOrderId": "EXT-20260723-0001",\n    "productId": 12,\n    "productName": "Starter Plan",\n    "amount": 99,\n    "currency": "CNY",\n    "status": "none",\n    "payStatus": "pending",\n    "payMethod": "alipay",\n    "tradeNo": null,\n    "createdAt": "2026-07-23T12:35:00.000Z",\n    "paidAt": null,\n    "returnUrl": "https://merchant.example.com/payment/success",\n    "cancelUrl": "https://merchant.example.com/payment/cancel",\n    "notifyUrl": "https://merchant.example.com/api/payment/notify",\n    "notify": null,\n    "attach": {\n      "userId": "u_1024",\n      "channel": "mobile_h5"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Paid Notification To `notifyUrl`\n\nWhen APayShop marks the order as paid, it sends a `POST` request to your `notifyUrl`.\n\nThis is triggered by:\n\n- payment gateway webhook success\n- admin-side manual payment confirmation\n\n### Notification Headers\n\n```http\nX-APayShop-Event: minimal.checkout.paid\nX-APayShop-Timestamp: 1721712345678\nX-APayShop-Signature: <hex-hmac-sha256>\nContent-Type: application/json\n```\n\n### Notification Signature\n\nFor outbound merchant notifications, the signature is:\n\n```text\nHMAC_SHA256(secret, timestamp + "\\n" + raw_json_body)\n```\n\n### Notification Body Example\n\n```json\n{\n  "event": "minimal.checkout.paid",\n  "timestamp": "2026-07-23T12:40:00.000Z",\n  "data": {\n    "orderId": "ON20260723981234AB12CD34",\n    "externalOrderId": "EXT-20260723-0001",\n    "amount": 99,\n    "currency": "CNY",\n    "status": "completed",\n    "payStatus": "paid",\n    "tradeNo": "2026072300019988",\n    "paidAt": "2026-07-23T12:39:45.000Z",\n    "deliveryInfo": null,\n    "contactEmail": "buyer@example.com",\n    "product": {\n      "id": 12,\n      "slug": "starter-plan",\n      "name": "Starter Plan",\n      "type": "one_time",\n      "price": 99\n    },\n    "attach": {\n      "userId": "u_1024",\n      "channel": "mobile_h5"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Browser Redirect Back To Merchant\n\nAfter payment succeeds or the user cancels checkout, APayShop can redirect the browser back to your system.\n\n### Success Redirect\n\nWhen `returnUrl` is configured, APayShop appends:\n\n- `orderId`\n- `externalOrderId`\n- `status=paid`\n\n### Cancel Redirect\n\nWhen `cancelUrl` is configured, APayShop appends:\n\n- `orderId`\n- `externalOrderId`\n- `status=cancelled` or `status=failed`\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nhttps://merchant.example.com/payment/success?orderId=ON...&externalOrderId=EXT-20260723-0001&status=paid\n```\n\n## Recommended Integration Strategy\n\n1. Use `externalOrderId` as your only merchant-side idempotency key.\n2. Open `checkoutUrl` in the browser directly.\n3. Treat `notifyUrl` as the source of truth for successful payment.\n4. Use `returnUrl` only for user experience, not as the final payment proof.\n5. If your server misses a callback, call `/api/minimal/checkout/status` with `externalOrderId` for reconciliation.\n';export{e as default};
